Date: Wed, 29 Dec 1993 16:10:22 -0800
From: plaz@netcom.com (Geoff Dale)
Subject: Anarchy PPL: Draft Proposal (RFC)

Some members of the extropians-list have expressed interest in a less
restrictive PPL than PPL-1. The PPL I am proposing here is designed to
fulfill that need.

This draft is a Request For Comments (RFC).

AnarchyPPL (PPL-A) Protections:
-------------------------------
First and foremost, PPL-A commits to do what a PPL is supposed to do,
protect its members. It will protect them from arbitrary judgments of other
PPLs and the effects of tempers of list members. The PPL will go to bat for
them as long as they stay within it's rules. The ExI-Board still has the
right to expel a person from the list, but the PPL promises to be it's
clients' advocate in that forum as well.

The PPL may look into being a mutual protection society. If it is felt that
unjust charges or actions are brought against its members, alternatives
will be discussed on how to use the membership (on a voluntary basis of
course) to redress the issue.

AnarchyPPL (PPL-A) Rules:
-------------------------
In accordance with the principles of anarchy and spontaneous order, this
PPL's rules are kept down to minimal levels, and netiquette is not
enforced. Politeness will grow from social interactions or the individual
will find himself ::excluded by just about everyone. The marketable
attribute of having something to say will counteract this effect on certain
individuals, but this is desirable as well.

Serious Offenses:
1> Spoofing and any other form of fraud including libel and slander.

2> Forwarding list messages to a third party (defined as a party not
either subscribed to the list, or a member ExI) without the author(s)
permission.

3> In addition, a formal complaint being made on a person for excessive and
repeated rudeness by a member of Anarchy-PPL or any other PPL.

The adjudicator will consider ejecting (from the PPL) or banning (from
posting for a period of time) any person who is accused of committing a
serious offense on a case-by-case basis, but never before cautioning the
person that he/she is treading the line and giving him/her the chance to
change his/her tune. If the person is deemed to have committed the offense
and it is deemed necessary by the adjudicator, the offender must post a
retraction or apology for the said offense. Failure to do so will result in
expulsion from the PPL.

If a member is ejected from the Anarchy PPL and no other PPL will take
him/her in, that member is effectively kicked off the list. Harry has made
it clear that you must belong to some PPL.

Minor Offenses:
1> The mandatory META, FORWARD/FWD, POLL, and PLEDGE prefixes.

2> Arguing against the basics, as strictly defined as:

        A> Statist arguments 
                Intermediate strategies explicate excepted.

        B> Deathist arguments
                'Nuff said.

        C> Religion-ist arguments
                Rational discussion of religious philosophies           
                explicitly excepted. Just don't push the faith, or 
                existence of gods, aspects. No flying yogis.

Minor offenders will be issued warnings until the point were it becomes a
serious offense type 3 (until someone brings a formal complaint). Warnings
previously issued may be considered the members "chance to change his/her
tune" at the adjudicator's discretion.

AnarchyPPL (PPL-A)
A Summary of what is allowed but wasn't allowed in PPL-1:
---------------------------------------------------------

Public plonkings, setting the facts straight, and defending one's honor
will explicitly be permitted. These, as a matter of fact, happen all the
time in PPL-1 with no one batting an eye. Judiciously used, these can act
as a powerful social feedback mechanism.

I personally still think that ad hominem attacks, me-too messages, and
utter cluelessness (aka newbie basics discussions) are bad things. I just
don't "think there ought to be a law". People can protect themselves from
this. This fine list software we now have especially empowers people to
::exclude idiots, and people who offend them.

Note that the "third party" has been defined as "a party not either
subscribed to the list, or a member ExI."

AnarchyPPL (PPL-A) What you can do now:
---------------------------------------
If you are interested in joining PPL-A, send private e-mail to me at
plaz@netcom.com, and cc: Harry Shapiro <habs@panix.com>, if you haven't
already. We need to know how many people are behind this concept.

In the first twenty-four hours 5 people (plus myself) have expressed interest.

I will repost this message + any revisions after the holiday season is
over. The finished proposal will be formally submitted to the ExI-Board
soon after that.

