their actual practice in consonance (or conflict) with them.  And it is 
often a revelation to meet, say, an author of serious articles, who 
does not apparently behave as one would expect from the impressions 
which they have made with their written work.   The conflict between 
the literal presentation of ideas and the actual interpretation of them 
says a lot to me, regarding the "meaning of meaning", and how we 
understand (think about) things.

